.claude/worktrees/

# Rust
/target/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Both forms: a worktree's `.venv` is a symlink, and `.venv/` matches only a
# directory, so the slashless line is what keeps `git add -A` from staging it
# (issue #556).
.venv
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.benchmarks/
.coverage
*.egg-info/
.ruff_cache/

# In-place compiled extension from `pip install -e .`
python/snakes_and_ladders/*.so
python/snakes_and_ladders/*.pyd
python/snakes_and_ladders/*.dylib

# Sphinx build output
docs/_build/

# LaTeX build output (the PDFs are built into docs/, not left here)
docs/tex/*.aux
docs/tex/*.bbl
docs/tex/*.blg
docs/tex/*.fdb_latexmk
docs/tex/*.fls
docs/tex/*.log
docs/tex/*.out
docs/tex/*.pdf
docs/tex/*.toc

# QA figures/captions under docs/tex/figures/ are committed, not ignored:
# they are the documents' evidence, and a reviewer should see a
# changed plot in the diff rather than have to build a document to find
# out. infra/build_documents.sh regenerates every cited figure (DEV.md).

# infra/build_documents.sh's LaTeX build output. The PDFs themselves
# are committed (see DEV.md); everything latexmk leaves beside them is not.
docs/*.aux
docs/*.bbl
docs/*.blg
docs/*.fdb_latexmk
docs/*.fls
docs/*.log
docs/*.out
docs/*.toc
docs/*.synctex.gz


# The generated ledgers (issue #425). CHECKS.md is written from the tests'
# own markers, SEAMS.md from the package, and the textbook's applicability
# tables from PROBLEMS.md and the suite. Committing them made a machine-
# written file a merge participant: on 2026-09-08 CHECKS.md conflicted on
# nine branches and resolving one carries no information. They are written
# by infra/ledgers.sh -- in the document build, at the release gate, and in
# CI, where regenerating them must change no tracked file.
# docs/tex/method_notes.yaml is hand-written and stays committed; it is an
# input to the tables, which is why it does not live under generated/.
/CHECKS.md
/SEAMS.md
/docs/tex/generated/
